<main class="page">
  <p class="eyebrow">Ironhold · Pre-release</p>
  <h1>Receive signed webhooks</h1>
  <p>
    Ironhold authenticates webhook requests, rejects exact replays, and stores accepted events
    idempotently in PostgreSQL.
  </p>
  <p>Built with Elixir, Phoenix, PostgreSQL, HMAC-SHA256, and ExUnit.</p>

  <section aria-labelledby="capabilities">
    <h2 id="capabilities">Implemented and tested</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Authenticate before storing:</strong> HMAC-SHA256 over the exact request bytes,
        timestamp verification, JSON content validation, and request size limits.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Separate retries from replays:</strong> cryptographic replay protection and
        idempotency by event ID, type, and payload, with transactional PostgreSQL persistence.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Maintain and observe:</strong> replay claim expiration and supervised cleanup,
        Telemetry events and metrics, and automated tests.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="responses">
    <h2 id="responses">Retries and replays</h2>
    <p>
      A legitimate retry with a fresh timestamp and signature is not an exact replay.
      <code>POST /api/webhooks</code>
      responds as follows for authenticated, valid envelopes:
    </p>
    <table aria-labelledby="responses">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Request</th>
          <th scope="col">Response</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>First valid webhook</td>
          <td>202 Accepted</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Same event ID, type, and payload with a fresh timestamp and signature</td>
          <td>202 Accepted</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Exact signature replay or the same event ID with conflicting content</td>
          <td>409 Conflict</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Both conflict cases return the same generic response. An accepted identical retry does not
      create another stored event.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="limitations">
    <h2 id="limitations">Pre-release limitations</h2>
    <p>
      Ingestion rate limiting, signing secret rotation, broader operational auditing and retention,
      a dashboard, external metrics reporting, and alerts remain future work. Production deployment
      is not proven; automated tests and green CI do not establish production readiness.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="documentation">
    <h2 id="documentation">Contract and companion project</h2>
    <p>
      Tidewake produces and sends webhooks; Ironhold is a complementary receiver. They are independent
      systems and repositories, with no proven joint production deployment.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a
        class="eyebrow"
        href="https://github.com/Carlos-ccaetano/Ironhold/blob/main/docs/api/webhooks.md"
      >
        HTTP contract
      </a>
      ·
      <a class="eyebrow" href="https://github.com/Carlos-ccaetano/Tidewake">Tidewake repository</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</main>
